 The SPL2/QPDL protocol implementation is derived from the GPLv2-licensed
 OpenPrinting SpliX project, so this driver is licensed to match.

Files: src/spl.rs
       src/main.rs
       ppd/samsung-ml2160.ppd
Copyright: 2025-2026 Çağan ERGÜN <73942784+caganerg@users.noreply.github.com>
           Aurélien Croc (AP²C) and the OpenPrinting SpliX contributors
License: GPL-2
 These three files carry material transcribed from OpenPrinting SpliX
 (https://github.com/OpenPrinting/splix), which is GPL-2.0-only. They are
 therefore a derived work and this package cannot be relicensed as GPL-2+.
 .
 src/spl.rs states the derivation in its own header: the QPDL wire constants,
 the PJL job header and its exact line order, the 17-byte page header layout
 and the Algo 0x11 RLE band encoding all come from SpliX's qpdl.cpp,
 compress.cpp, algo0x11.cpp and printer.cpp.
 .
 src/main.rs transcribes SpliX's geometry rules, each cited at the function
 that implements it: the page-width computation from document.cpp, the hard
 margin and column-major band fill from compress.cpp _compressBandedPage, the
 duplex mapping from request.cpp, and the "halve the band height at 300x300"
 rule from compress.cpp.
 .
 ppd/samsung-ml2160.ppd takes its QPDL paper-source codes, media-type
 keywords and band size from the sibling PPDs upstream SpliX ships for this
 engine family (ml1910, ml2010, ml2525, ml1640, ml2510), as its own comments
 record.
 .
 src/raster.rs and src/golden.rs are NOT derived from SpliX: raster.rs
 implements the CUPS Raster container format, and golden.rs is this project's
 own test harness. Each mentions SpliX once, as a cross-reference rather than
 as transcribed material.
Comment: The upstream attribution above names the SpliX author and project but
 omits the year range, because the exact copyright notice must be transcribed
 from the SpliX source headers and no copy of that source was available on the
 machine where this stanza was written. Before the first upload, copy the
 notice verbatim from the upstream tree.

Files: crates/pappl-sys/*
